p('The laptop GPU has 6 GB memory and is below the allowed RTX 4090 limit. It was used only for training; no additional pretrained weights were obtained. Neural training from scratch and in-domain language pretraining use only supplied training data. CUDA runtime installation is a software dependency, not a pretrained language model. Family times include different preprocessing/search scopes and some jobs overlap, so they must not be summed as a total project wall time.')
p('Official data hashes and evaluator files were checked. The released checkpoint reproduces the recorded prediction choices. Eleven validation questions with new IDs and candidate permutations preserve selected numeric answers. Four-decimal tree input rounding limits sensitivity to small floating-point changes; this finite smoke check is not a proof for every input. Separate CPU retraining smoke runs completed for both selected extensions; cross-device retraining need not reproduce the frozen weights or score exactly.')
page();title('Reproduce, disclose and submit')
heading('7. Frozen result reproduction')
p('From code/, install requirements.txt in an isolated Python environment, then set OMP_NUM_THREADS, OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS, MKL_NUM_THREADS and NUMEXPR_NUM_THREADS to 4. The main README supplies exact PowerShell commands. No retraining is needed to reproduce the claimed score.')
p('<font name="Courier" size="8">python check_data.py<br/><br/>python predict.py --method submission_v6.py --checkpoint runs/final --split test --output runs/reproduced-v6-predictions.json<br/><br/>python score_predictions.py --split test --predictions runs/reproduced-v6-predictions.json --output runs/reproduced-v6-score.json</font>')
p('Expected official accuracy is <b>83.08351177730192</b>. runs/v6-test-score.json is the official result, v6-resources.json records complete external timing, v6-checks.json records checks, and frozen_v6.json identifies all frozen inference assets and source hashes. Its test_evaluated=false field describes the state at freeze time; subsequent official scoring is recorded separately. It is not a claim that the reported version has never been tested.')
heading('Training reproduction')
p('train_all.ps1 replays original baseline development using the supplied training/validation splits. train_v4.ps1 rebuilds the alignment extension in a separate output. train_v5.py --device cpu --output runs/retrained_v5 rebuilds the selected pairwise extension; --device cuda uses the GPU training path. train_v6.py --device CPU --output runs/retrained_v6 rebuilds the semantic ranker while retaining the supplied frozen baseline; --device GPU uses its GPU path. Both selected-extension CPU commands were executed successfully locally.')
p('The training-only neural out-of-fold cache is retained under runs/v2 and can be regenerated by train_stack.py. build_v3_oof.py recreates the next-stage training cache. code/v4 contains research scripts and detailed records for positive and negative studies. Development scripts may require preceding feature-building steps; TRAINING.md lists their order. Fixed released weights, rather than cross-device retraining, are the claimed-score reproduction target.')
heading('AI, reuse and submission status')
p('OpenAI Codex substantially assisted with architecture and feature design, code, training, experiment selection, analysis and report preparation. The student must review and understand the implementation and results. Supplied evaluation tools and data were retained unchanged. GSM8K-derived questions and references retain the supplied MIT license and attribution. Candidate solutions and fixed representations were prepared by the course using Qwen3-0.6B. No external datasets or additional pretrained weights were used.')
p('No public repository, checkpoint URL or GitHub submission issue has been created. Student ID and a public destination have not been supplied. Final submission requires code and checkpoint/configuration links, then actual creation of the GitHub issue prepared by the course website before <b>31 October 2026, 23:59 UTC+8</b>. If submitting this V6 version, self-report its official test score above, with submission_v6.py and the matching runs/final checkpoint. Validation accuracy must not be self-reported as test accuracy.')
